{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":18,"code":"JOB","name":"Job","testament":"OT"},"chapter":30,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"JOB 30:1"},"But now ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["they that are"]}," younger than I have me in derision, whose fathers I would have disdained to have set with the dogs of my flock. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:1"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"JOB 30:2"},"Yea, whereto ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["might"]}," the strength of their hands ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["profit "]},"me, in whom old age was perished? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:2"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"JOB 30:3"},"For want and famine ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["they were"]}," solitary; fleeing into the wilderness in former time desolate and waste. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:3"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"JOB 30:4"},"Who cut up mallows by the bushes, and juniper roots ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["for"]}," their meat. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:4"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"JOB 30:5"},"They were driven forth from among ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["men,"]}," (they cried after them as ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["after"]}," a thief;) ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:5"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"JOB 30:6"},"To dwell in the cliffs of the valleys, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["in"]}," caves of the earth, and ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["in"]}," the rocks. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:6"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"JOB 30:7"},"Among the bushes they brayed; under the nettles they were gathered together. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:7"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"JOB 30:8"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["They were"]}," children of fools, yea, children of base men: they were viler than the earth. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:8"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"JOB 30:9"},"And now am I their song, yea, I am their byword. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:9"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"JOB 30:10"},"They abhor me, they flee far from me, and spare not to spit in my face. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:10"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"JOB 30:11"},"Because he hath loosed my cord, and afflicted me, they have also let loose the bridle before me. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:11"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"JOB 30:12"},"Upon ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["my"]}," right ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["hand"]}," rise the youth; they push away my feet, and they raise up against me the ways of their destruction. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:12"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"JOB 30:13"},"They mar my path, they set forward my calamity, they have no helper. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:13"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"JOB 30:14"},"They came ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["upon me"]}," as a wide breaking in ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["of waters: "]},"in the desolation they rolled themselves ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["upon me. "]},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:14"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"15","sid":"JOB 30:15"},"Terrors are turned upon me: they pursue my soul as the wind: and my welfare passeth away as a cloud. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:15"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"16","sid":"JOB 30:16"},"And now my soul is poured out upon me; the days of affliction have taken hold upon me. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:16"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"17","sid":"JOB 30:17"},"My bones are pierced in me in the night season: and my sinews take no rest. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:17"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"18","sid":"JOB 30:18"},"By the great force ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["of my disease"]}," is my garment changed: it bindeth me about as the collar of my coat. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:18"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"19","sid":"JOB 30:19"},"He hath cast me into the mire, and I am become like dust and ashes. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:19"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"20","sid":"JOB 30:20"},"I cry unto thee, and thou dost not hear me: I stand up, and thou regardest me ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["not. "]},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:20"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"21","sid":"JOB 30:21"},"Thou art become cruel to me: with thy strong hand thou opposest thyself against me. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:21"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"22","sid":"JOB 30:22"},"Thou liftest me up to the wind; thou causest me to ride ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["upon it, "]},"and dissolvest my substance. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:22"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"23","sid":"JOB 30:23"},"For I know ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["that"]}," thou wilt bring me ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["to"]}," death, and ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["to"]}," the house appointed for all living. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:23"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"24","sid":"JOB 30:24"},"Howbeit he will not stretch out ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["his"]}," hand to the grave, though they cry in his destruction. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:24"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"25","sid":"JOB 30:25"},"Did not I weep for him that was in trouble? was ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["not"]}," my soul grieved for the poor? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:25"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"26","sid":"JOB 30:26"},"When I looked for good, then evil came ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["unto me:"]}," and when I waited for light, there came darkness. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:26"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"27","sid":"JOB 30:27"},"My bowels boiled, and rested not: the days of affliction prevented me. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:27"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"28","sid":"JOB 30:28"},"I went mourning without the sun: I stood up, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," I cried in the congregation. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:28"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"29","sid":"JOB 30:29"},"I am a brother to dragons, and a companion to owls. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:29"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"30","sid":"JOB 30:30"},"My skin is black upon me, and my bones are burned with heat. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:30"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"31","sid":"JOB 30:31"},"My harp also is ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["turned"]}," to mourning, and my organ into the voice of them that weep. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 30:31"}]}]}
